Rosalind, Nathaniel,<br />
<br />
Halstead called yesterday to pin down the shape of the commitment before Va=
ndergrift signs anything. My recommendation is that we take what he is offe=
ring.<br />
<br />
He will give us the account transfers, the discontinuation of the debit ins=
truction, and surprise examinations with Form ADV-E filings for 2011 and 20=
12, all of it in writing and all of it specific. What he will not give us i=
s an open-ended forward commitment. His argument is that this firm has 742 =
accounts, one office, no acquisition history and no pipeline, so an indefin=
ite undertaking would be policing a risk that does not exist here.<br />
<br />
I think that is right on these facts. The exposure at this firm is the tran=
sition, not the future. Two full calendar years of surprise examinations ge=
ts us past the transition and gives us an ADV-E filing to look at on the re=
cord. If the practice ever comes back, we would be examining the conduct it=
self under the rule, and we would not need an undertaking to do it.<br />
<br />
Recommend we accept a commitment expressed for calendar years 2011 and 2012=
.<br />
<br />
Desmond